examples.example:
In an example used by Sigmund Freud in *The Interpretation of Dreams*, a man accused by his neighbor of having returned a kettle in a damaged condition offered three arguments:

That he had returned the kettle undamaged;
That it was already damaged when he borrowed it;
That he had never borrowed it in the first place.

examples_et.example:
Sigmund Freudi raamatus *Unenägude tõlgendamine* kasutatud näites esitas mees, keda tema naaber süüdistas kahjustatud seisukorras veekeetja tagastamises, kolm argumenti:

Et ta oli tagastanud veekeetja kahjustamata;
Et see oli juba laenamisel kahjustatud;
Et ta polnud seda kunagi laenanud.

